      "body": "## Overview\n\n`vllm bench serve --backend openai-audio` reports the wrong input token count for every transcription request. The audio datasets set `prompt_len` from a text prompt the request never sends, and the client ignores `usage.prompt_tokens`. This reads `prompt_tokens` from the usage chunk, as the completions and chat clients already do.\n\n## Claims\n\n- On Whisper the bench reported 8 input tokens per request, the tokens of the dataset prompt \"Transcribe the audio.\". The server reports `100 × audio seconds + 4` (304 for a 3 s clip, 2,504 for 25 s).\n- Total input tokens now match the server. Output tokens were already correct.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test in `tests/benchmarks/test_endpoint_request_func_timing.py`, over the completions, chat and audio clients: `prompt_len` takes the server's usage value. It fails for audio on `main`. `tests/benchmarks/` passes (194) and pre-commit is clean.\n\nRTX 3080, `openai/whisper-tiny`, 18 clips from 3 s to 25 s cut from vLLM's `mary_had_lamb` and `winning_call` test assets, `--dataset-name custom_audio`:\n\n| | `main` | this branch | server `usage.prompt_tokens` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| total input tokens | 144 | 21,757 | 21,757 |\n\nTotal token throughput is computed from total input tokens, so it rises with this change. Request rate and output tokens are unchanged. The request on the wire carries no prompt field.\n\n## Details\n\nThe server's `vllm:prompt_tokens_total` metric rose by 72 on the same run, 4 per request, so it counts the decoder prompt without the audio, while `usage` counts both. I left that alone; the bench follows `usage` as it does for the other backends.\n\nThe legacy `benchmarks/backend_request_func.py` reads `prompt_tokens` for no backend, so it is out of scope.\n\nNo issue or PR covers this. AI assistance (Claude) was used to find this and write the change and test. I reviewed every line and ran the tests and GPU comparison.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
